        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): filter device and internal sessions from thread picker",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid thread picker showed device/internal sessions such as `agent:main:node-*`, `agent:main:main`, and onboarding keys that iOS already hides via `CommandCenterTab.isRecentChatSession`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd `isSelectableChatSession` parity with iOS and filter those keys in `resolveSessionChoices` while preserving pinned main/current behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRecent session choices are cleaner and match iOS session list behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Unit tests**\n- `SessionFiltersTest.sessionChoicesFilterAgentDeviceAndInternalSessions`\n- `SessionFiltersTest.isSelectableChatSession_matchesIosRecentSessionFilter`\n\n**Local proof (Windows, branch `48222962a9`)**\n```powershell\ncd apps/android\n.\\gradlew.bat :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.chat.SessionFiltersTest\n```\n- Result: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 9m 27s` (first Gradle/SDK warmup)\n- JUnit: 5 tests, 0 failures (`SessionFiltersTest`)\n\n**Note:** Emulator/device screenshot proof for the visible picker is not included in this PR; unit tests cover the filtering helper used by both picker surfaces.\n",
